WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
[moody, intense intro music plays]

01:18.620 --> 01:20.789
[phone] Toll fees have been charged.

01:20.872 --> 01:22.874
[gentle pop ballad playing]

01:30.590 --> 01:36.971
♪ Still one thing puzzles me inside ♪

01:39.682 --> 01:44.604
♪ Why can't I live a normal life? ♪

01:44.687 --> 01:45.688
SUMMER OF 2022

01:47.941 --> 01:52.821
♪ No matter how hard I try ♪

01:52.904 --> 01:56.783
♪ To change myself ♪

01:57.450 --> 01:58.660
♪ I know ♪

02:00.703 --> 02:04.415
♪ This much is true ♪

02:06.709 --> 02:12.632
♪ How can I bring peace to my heart? ♪

02:15.677 --> 02:19.472
♪ I think about it ♪

02:19.556 --> 02:23.309
♪ Every day ♪

02:24.018 --> 02:28.439
♪ I don't want to pretend ♪

02:28.523 --> 02:30.692
♪ To be good ♪

02:30.775 --> 02:32.610
JAEPYEONG CONSTRUCTION

02:33.111 --> 02:35.864
♪ Anymore ♪

02:35.947 --> 02:39.534
♪ No longer ♪

02:42.537 --> 02:46.666
♪ I've been through a lot ♪

02:46.749 --> 02:50.503
♪ My whole life ♪

02:51.379 --> 02:52.839
♪ I felt like ♪

02:52.922 --> 02:58.803
♪ There was no more chance ♪

03:03.391 --> 03:05.852
EDEN APARTMENTS

03:05.935 --> 03:11.816
♪ They taught me how to live again ♪

03:14.152 --> 03:21.117
♪ And never fall into despair ♪

03:22.493 --> 03:26.789
♪ I just want to live ♪

03:26.873 --> 03:31.044
♪ A long life ♪

03:31.544 --> 03:34.297
♪ From now on ♪

03:35.173 --> 03:40.970
♪ Till the end of ♪

03:42.055 --> 03:44.641
♪ From now on… ♪

03:44.724 --> 03:46.267
[woman] Did you just move in?

03:46.768 --> 03:47.769
[song stops]

03:51.814 --> 03:52.982
Hi, how are you?

03:53.483 --> 03:56.361
Oh. Finally, you're here now.

03:56.444 --> 03:58.112
You sure took your time.

04:01.991 --> 04:02.992
Anyway, welcome.

04:03.076 --> 04:06.287
This flower here is known as
the Devil's Trumpet.

04:06.371 --> 04:08.414
That one there is called
the Angel's Trumpet

04:08.498 --> 04:10.917
'cause it looks like
a horn facing the ground.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.710
That one is the Devil's Trumpet

04:12.794 --> 04:15.255
because it looks like
a horn playing into the sky.

04:15.338 --> 04:18.549
[chuckles] Apparently, God thought
they were cocky for looking up.

04:18.633 --> 04:22.637
Maybe that's the reason
why you can only smell them at nighttime.

04:24.472 --> 04:28.017
You need to shatter these kinds of pots
before you can toss them.

04:28.101 --> 04:29.227
-[shatters]
-[crunches loudly]

04:29.310 --> 04:30.728
[flame whooshes]

04:33.273 --> 04:35.358
[slow, unsettling music playing]

04:52.000 --> 04:53.626
[woman] My dear Yeon-jin…

04:53.710 --> 04:54.752
TO YEON-JIN

04:54.836 --> 04:56.254
Do you remember

04:57.171 --> 05:00.091
that I used to hate the summer?

05:00.174 --> 05:01.259
[staple gun firing]

05:02.260 --> 05:05.763
Thankfully, I moved away
before it got even hotter.

05:06.889 --> 05:08.599
I've been organizing these photos,

05:09.600 --> 05:13.271
but it's taking so long
because of all these friendly faces.

05:13.354 --> 05:14.731
WEATHERCASTER PARK YEON-JIN

05:14.814 --> 05:17.108
And every time I start going through them,

05:17.191 --> 05:20.028
I picture you opening that door.

05:20.111 --> 05:21.237
[tense music playing]

05:21.321 --> 05:22.322
[woman chuckles]

05:26.326 --> 05:27.160
Wow.

05:30.163 --> 05:31.164
What are you doing?

05:31.831 --> 05:35.084
That's Jae-jun… Sa-ra… Photos of everyone…

05:36.502 --> 05:37.420
So then,

05:38.838 --> 05:39.672
who are you?

05:43.468 --> 05:45.470
It's me, Yeon-jin. Me.

05:47.764 --> 05:49.849
You really haven't changed at all, huh?

05:51.059 --> 05:52.894
You still have no manners, do you?

05:52.977 --> 05:56.147
You should take your shoes off
when you enter somebody's home.

05:58.024 --> 05:58.983
[stapler gun rattles]

05:59.942 --> 06:01.569
[panting]

06:01.652 --> 06:03.071
[breathing heavily]

06:04.697 --> 06:06.949
Now, I have
yet another reason to kill you.

06:07.033 --> 06:08.910
You should at least recognize who I am.

06:09.494 --> 06:11.496
[cackles]

06:11.579 --> 06:13.873
Kill me? You think you could kill me?

06:13.956 --> 06:14.957
Yeah, I know so.

06:15.958 --> 06:18.461
I know I'm going to do my best
to try and kill you.

06:19.545 --> 06:21.130
So go and get ready, Yeon-jin.

06:21.923 --> 06:23.174
I'm already here for you.

06:23.758 --> 06:24.634
[stapler gun clicks]

06:24.717 --> 06:25.718
Ah.

06:26.969 --> 06:30.056
Do you want to hear the whole story

06:30.139 --> 06:34.102
and how… I got here?

06:36.938 --> 06:37.772
CHIEF SHIN YEONG-JUN

06:37.855 --> 06:39.482
Since an official report has been filed,

06:39.565 --> 06:41.692
we'll have to follow procedure
and call their guardians.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.779
But don't worry,
I'll make sure she gets off easy.

06:44.862 --> 06:46.197
SUMMER OF 2004

06:46.280 --> 06:47.323
I'll call you later.

06:49.575 --> 06:50.410
Park Yeon-jin…

06:52.829 --> 06:54.580
-Yeah?
-Why were you bullying your friend?

06:54.664 --> 06:56.332
I don't want you here for that again.

06:56.416 --> 06:59.502
-Your mother's been told. Get going.
-But she's not my friend.

06:59.585 --> 07:03.423
By the way, sir,
what's going on between you and my mother?

07:04.507 --> 07:05.633
We're friends from childhood.

07:06.467 --> 07:08.803
Oh, you're like Son Myeong-o?

07:08.886 --> 07:11.389
So that's why you've been
so helpful with her divorce.

07:11.472 --> 07:14.183
You're the one who proved
my dad was having an affair.

07:14.267 --> 07:17.395
I was wrong.
I was thinking you slept with her.

07:17.478 --> 07:19.313
-[Yeon-jin laughs]
-[door opens, closes]

07:23.025 --> 07:24.026
[woman] Get up!

07:24.569 --> 07:26.821
All the deliveries are
gonna be backed up. Go!

07:26.904 --> 07:29.157
Come on. I told you not to come, asshole.

07:29.240 --> 07:32.326
[woman 2] All you two need to do is
just hug and say sorry.

07:32.410 --> 07:33.786
Come on, Sa-ra. Let's go.

07:34.954 --> 07:37.165
[siren wailing]

07:37.248 --> 07:38.499
[woman] …mentioned a car?

07:38.583 --> 07:39.750
[exhales heavily]

07:40.626 --> 07:41.961
[phone ringing]

07:44.714 --> 07:45.965
How can I help you, sir?

07:46.048 --> 07:48.676
[man] I'm acting as her legal guardian.
I'm her teacher.

07:49.760 --> 07:51.762
[inhales, sighs]

07:52.889 --> 07:53.723
Hey.

07:54.307 --> 07:56.225
What the hell are you doing
at the police station?

07:56.309 --> 07:59.061
You thought it was a good idea to call
the police over some small prank?

07:59.145 --> 08:00.688
The vice principal found out--

08:01.355 --> 08:03.316
[inhales, sighs]

08:03.399 --> 08:05.568
We'll talk later. Come on. Let's go.

08:05.651 --> 08:07.153
[boy] Sir, help me too.

08:07.236 --> 08:08.613
I'm an orphan this week

08:09.822 --> 08:12.783
'cause my parents are abroad… golfing.

08:12.867 --> 08:13.868
Really?

08:14.744 --> 08:17.079
You should have called me
as soon as you could.

08:17.580 --> 08:18.748
I'll take him, too.

08:18.831 --> 08:20.082
[officer] Oh, yeah. Sure.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.669
[teacher] I was wondering,
why are you still here?

08:23.753 --> 08:25.379
Wait. Who's making your meals?

08:25.463 --> 08:27.882
-[boy] Our housekeeper.
-[teacher] Oh, of course.

08:27.965 --> 08:29.592
[tense music swells, fades away]

08:33.888 --> 08:36.140
[woman] Didn't I say today was important?

08:36.224 --> 08:38.726
I am so disappointed by what you did.

08:40.311 --> 08:44.232
-I didn't know I'd get in trouble.
-[woman] And that's why I'm disappointed.

08:44.815 --> 08:46.567
You couldn't handle someone so low.

08:47.235 --> 08:48.653
[woman grunting angrily]

08:50.029 --> 08:52.698
Didn't I say
that you can only hang out with Jae-jun?

08:52.782 --> 08:53.908
If you're bored, Sa-ra too.

08:55.451 --> 08:56.452
Did you forget?

08:57.495 --> 09:00.289
The shaman said you'd get bad luck
from people with Os in their name.

09:01.123 --> 09:03.876
Son Myeong-o. Choi Hye-jeong.
I'm talking about those kids now!

09:04.877 --> 09:06.712
Inside. We're running late.

09:06.796 --> 09:08.798
[drums, percussive instruments banging]

09:10.883 --> 09:13.094
[woman vocalizing]

09:25.398 --> 09:27.400
[continues vocalizing]

09:50.506 --> 09:51.591
[phone chimes]

09:55.720 --> 09:58.139
MOON DONG-EUN
SUNGHAN HIGH SCHOOL

10:06.647 --> 10:07.982
Dong-eun's here!

10:08.065 --> 10:10.026
The one that you get to see every day.

10:10.109 --> 10:11.652
[boy chuckles]

10:13.654 --> 10:14.905
[boy laughs]

10:15.489 --> 10:16.490
[Yeon-jin] Welcome!

10:18.701 --> 10:20.286
[Dong-eun whimpers]

10:20.369 --> 10:22.622
[Yeon-jin] I wanted to apologize
for bullying you.

10:22.705 --> 10:25.708
I'm sorry. We even now?

10:27.752 --> 10:31.130
There was no need to call the cops on us,
was there? We got scared.

10:33.633 --> 10:35.134
Speaking of which, Dong-eun…

10:37.136 --> 10:38.387
from this moment on,

10:39.555 --> 10:41.140
you'll check if my iron is hot enough.

10:42.642 --> 10:44.769
-[menacing music plays]
-[panicked whimper]

10:45.353 --> 10:46.896
Please don't! No!

10:47.563 --> 10:49.565
They'll arrest you! Let go! Stop!

10:49.649 --> 10:53.027
Hey, now, what's the crime
in asking for a little favor?

10:53.110 --> 10:54.820
You're making us feel weird.

10:55.404 --> 10:57.239
Come on, check if it's hot or not.

10:57.323 --> 10:58.491
[Yeon-jin] Come on.

10:58.574 --> 11:00.409
-[flesh sizzling]
-[Dong-eun wails]

11:02.578 --> 11:04.246
[Yeon-jin] Is it hot enough?

11:06.957 --> 11:08.250
Seems to be good.

11:09.001 --> 11:10.002
Try it now.

11:10.086 --> 11:11.295
[Dong-eun sobbing]

11:12.129 --> 11:16.467
Somebody help me!
Somebody please come and save me!

11:17.259 --> 11:19.261
[girl] You're just wasting your time.

11:19.345 --> 11:21.472
Scream as loud as you can. No one'll come.

11:21.555 --> 11:23.307
Nobody will save you.

11:25.518 --> 11:27.478
The gym teacher even gave us the key!

11:27.561 --> 11:28.396
GYM

11:28.479 --> 11:29.939
[dark, overwhelming music playing]

11:35.194 --> 11:36.821
Why are you doing this?

11:37.947 --> 11:40.199
Why are you doing this to me? Please!

11:40.908 --> 11:42.493
I'm so sick of that.

11:44.412 --> 11:45.913
Why do you people always ask that?

11:46.497 --> 11:48.999
I do it because nothing
will ever happen to me,

11:49.083 --> 11:50.751
and nothing will change no matter what.

11:51.335 --> 11:52.461
Take now, for example.

11:52.545 --> 11:55.923
You raised such a fuss with the police,
but look where you are right now.

11:56.799 --> 11:58.259
Did anything change?

11:59.009 --> 12:01.971
What I'm trying to say is that
no one's going to save you.

12:02.471 --> 12:05.266
Not the cops, not the school,
not even your parents.

12:05.933 --> 12:07.893
Know what they call a person like that?

12:08.644 --> 12:10.521
They're called a loser.

12:11.313 --> 12:13.399
[bullies laughing]

12:13.983 --> 12:15.526
Did I hear you really live at a motel?

12:15.609 --> 12:18.320
I thought that you never
really had a home, no?

12:18.404 --> 12:20.614
It's like something out of a fairy tale.

12:21.449 --> 12:23.743
Guess you're living
in a fairy-tale, Dong-eun.

12:23.826 --> 12:27.246
Wow, I guess that makes her
my fairy godmother, then.

12:27.329 --> 12:29.999
Since she helped me check my iron.
Didn't she?

12:30.082 --> 12:31.542
-[flesh sizzling]
-[Dong-eun screams]

12:33.669 --> 12:35.337
Please, no! [Dong-eun whimpers]

12:35.421 --> 12:36.672
Let go!

12:37.339 --> 12:39.550
-[Dong-eun] No!
-Shut her up, will you Myeong-o?

12:39.633 --> 12:40.718
[Dong-eun] No!

12:42.470 --> 12:44.889
Hey, try and use your inside voice, okay?

12:46.223 --> 12:48.225
[dark, overwhelming music continues]

13:00.905 --> 13:02.531
[bullies cackling]

13:03.741 --> 13:05.743
[music trails off]

13:08.746 --> 13:10.247
[woman] Hydrogen peroxide?

13:11.624 --> 13:13.292
I spilled something on my shirt.

13:13.793 --> 13:15.795
If I can have some, I'll clean it up.

13:15.878 --> 13:17.546
[woman] What'd you get on your shirt?

13:18.756 --> 13:20.633
So you're… bleeding?

13:24.011 --> 13:26.096
Just let me have some hydrogen peroxide.

13:29.099 --> 13:30.100
[gasps]

13:30.851 --> 13:33.395
How did this happen? Who did this to you?

13:33.979 --> 13:35.856
Did you tell your homeroom teacher?

13:37.149 --> 13:39.068
I've seen something like this before.

13:39.568 --> 13:43.155
If you can't do it alone, I'll go with you
and tell your teacher. Okay?

13:43.656 --> 13:44.824
Who did it?

13:47.117 --> 13:49.119
[cheerful ringtone chiming]

13:59.255 --> 14:00.464
[Yeon-jin] Oh, hey, Mom.

14:01.632 --> 14:03.133
Can I call you back soon?

14:03.217 --> 14:05.219
[tense music playing]

14:07.096 --> 14:08.097
I did.

14:09.932 --> 14:11.642
Last time was me as well.

14:22.236 --> 14:23.445
[woman] Did you know, Yeon-jin…

14:26.448 --> 14:30.870
that your daughter likes
to look at the world upside-down?

14:33.038 --> 14:35.374
Maybe people can still understand

14:36.083 --> 14:37.751
because in some way,

14:37.835 --> 14:39.628
the whole world is always upside-down.

14:39.712 --> 14:41.213
[solemn choral music playing]

14:45.426 --> 14:48.846
Those look like
the same shoes my mom wears.

14:56.979 --> 14:58.063
So, you're her.

14:58.772 --> 15:01.275
Park Yeon-jin's daughter. Ha Ye-sol.

15:02.026 --> 15:03.444
Do you know who my mom is?

15:04.737 --> 15:06.906
I think about your mom every single day.

15:08.115 --> 15:11.493
There's a type of hatred
that's similar to longing.

15:12.369 --> 15:13.704
It's impossible to stop.

15:14.705 --> 15:16.707
Don't know hatred.

15:17.374 --> 15:18.459
What's it mean?

15:24.798 --> 15:26.300
You wanna know what hatred is?

15:33.223 --> 15:34.224
[wind whistling]

15:40.606 --> 15:42.608
[baby crying in distance]

15:51.367 --> 15:53.827
[faint laughter]

15:58.499 --> 16:00.084
[girl laughing] That's so fucking funny.

16:00.167 --> 16:01.168
[door opens]

16:10.469 --> 16:11.470
Huh.

16:11.971 --> 16:12.972
Hey.

16:13.973 --> 16:14.807
Leaving?

16:22.690 --> 16:24.692
[breathing shakily]

16:26.068 --> 16:28.696
[distressing music playing]

16:33.075 --> 16:36.161
[woman] Her eyes would darken
when she was having fun.

16:36.245 --> 16:37.913
What took you so long?

16:39.498 --> 16:41.291
I really missed you.

16:41.375 --> 16:43.502
[woman] Her lips curled up
when she smiled.

16:44.003 --> 16:46.463
All that dark, beautiful hair.

16:47.589 --> 16:48.924
If you put that together,

16:49.967 --> 16:51.719
that's what hatred looks like.

16:52.386 --> 16:54.388
[Dong-eun breathing tremulously]

16:55.055 --> 16:56.098
[bully laughs]

16:56.181 --> 16:58.851
No fucking way!
She took her shoes off. [cackles]

16:58.934 --> 17:01.603
Oh, we're so shitty. Shame on us.

17:02.104 --> 17:03.105
Move over.

17:04.106 --> 17:04.940
[Myeong-o] Hey!

17:05.524 --> 17:06.442
This your piggy bank?

17:06.525 --> 17:08.777
I found this in your rice cooker.

17:09.278 --> 17:11.739
-I just couldn't believe it.
-Give it to me.

17:13.949 --> 17:14.950
Oh, no.

17:16.035 --> 17:17.327
Are you mad at me?

17:18.287 --> 17:19.580
[grunts] Nice catch, huh?

17:20.164 --> 17:21.915
Wow. There's a ton in here.

17:21.999 --> 17:25.294
[bully] Ooh, that's it? So sad.

17:25.377 --> 17:29.965
[weeping sarcastically]
Dong-eun, you have such a terrible life.

17:30.549 --> 17:33.343
[Myeong-o] What's that crazy bitch on now?
Pan Cold or glue?

17:33.427 --> 17:35.179
-[plastic ripping]
-[Dong-eun] No!

17:35.262 --> 17:38.307
Stop! No! No!

17:38.390 --> 17:39.641
[overlapping clamoring]

17:39.725 --> 17:42.644
[Myeong-o] She's got so much dough!
This is like 200,000 won.

17:42.728 --> 17:44.313
Guess she's paying for all this?

17:44.396 --> 17:48.233
You guys all have money!
You guys don't need any of mine!

17:50.652 --> 17:52.905
Please, I'm begging you. Give it back.

17:52.988 --> 17:56.533
Hmm. Seems like
you've learned to behave, Dong-eun.

17:56.617 --> 17:57.618
Fine.

17:59.661 --> 18:00.662
I'll give it back.

18:02.748 --> 18:05.167
But you'll need to dance for us
while we drink.

18:05.250 --> 18:07.836
Then I won't touch any of it. Sound good?

18:08.378 --> 18:10.380
-What?
-Go and dance for us.

18:11.423 --> 18:14.009
How are we supposed to have fun
if no one's dancing?

18:15.094 --> 18:17.262
Don't you want it?

18:19.681 --> 18:22.601
Well, if you won't do that,
there's another way to get it.

18:23.560 --> 18:25.062
I found this in your house.

18:27.564 --> 18:29.775
You seem like a bit of a mess right now.

18:30.275 --> 18:32.653
And if you act like
you're better than this,

18:33.487 --> 18:36.949
you're going to have
a really, really big mess. Huh?

18:38.158 --> 18:39.493
So dance for me.

18:40.786 --> 18:42.162
Have some fun.

18:43.038 --> 18:44.373
[Yeon-jin giggles]

18:44.873 --> 18:46.875
It's fine if you don't want to.

18:49.878 --> 18:52.548
Hey, I've never noticed, but Dong-eun…

18:56.635 --> 18:57.719
your legs are pretty.

19:00.806 --> 19:02.808
[distressing music builds]

19:04.143 --> 19:05.144
[Yeon-jin snickers]

19:07.312 --> 19:08.814
[bully] I'll pick out the first song!

19:09.314 --> 19:11.650
I have a ton that are so fucking good.

19:11.733 --> 19:12.818
[giggles]

19:14.528 --> 19:15.904
[upbeat electronic music playing]

19:22.119 --> 19:23.620
[Dong-eun screams]

19:24.079 --> 19:26.999
[Dong-eun continues screaming faintly]

19:27.082 --> 19:28.917
[upbeat electronic music continuing]

19:33.797 --> 19:37.593
HEALTH OFFICE

19:43.348 --> 19:46.268
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
DUE TO RESIGNATION OF THE SCHOOL NURSE

19:48.520 --> 19:51.899
[somber, melancholy music playing]

19:52.900 --> 19:54.234
[squeaky rattling]

19:57.404 --> 19:59.406
[wind whistling]

20:37.486 --> 20:39.488
[music intensifies]

20:56.213 --> 20:57.214
[whimpers]

20:58.799 --> 21:01.343
[melancholy music continues]

22:02.821 --> 22:04.823
[whimpering, weeping]

22:28.263 --> 22:30.182
For real? When though?

22:32.142 --> 22:33.435
I'll call you back later.

22:36.104 --> 22:38.273
Hey… Dong-eun dropped out.

22:39.024 --> 22:41.401
And she listed us
as the reason for her transfer.

22:41.902 --> 22:43.236
She gave it to the vice principal,

22:43.320 --> 22:45.572
and now he's chewing out
our homeroom teacher.

22:47.699 --> 22:48.950
Not the gym teacher?

22:49.034 --> 22:52.120
She list us in order? [chuckles]

22:53.080 --> 22:55.123
I wonder where my name is on that list.

22:55.624 --> 22:57.709
Are you stupid or something?

23:01.797 --> 23:04.132
Hey! Jae-jun! Yeon-jin!

23:04.800 --> 23:05.801
Get over here!

23:13.558 --> 23:14.768
[man] You stupid fucking bitch!

23:15.769 --> 23:17.771
You should've just quietly dropped out.

23:17.854 --> 23:20.440
So you're innocent?
You didn't do anything wrong?

23:20.524 --> 23:23.068
Only someone this messed up
would push it this far!

23:23.151 --> 23:25.362
Come back and correct your reason,
right now!

23:25.862 --> 23:26.863
[disconnect tone chirps]

23:33.245 --> 23:35.997
DROPOUT FORM

23:36.081 --> 23:37.916
[man] If the principal finds out,

23:37.999 --> 23:40.419
it might affect
your performance review, Mr. Kim.

23:41.253 --> 23:43.255
I know that. Jesus.

23:43.338 --> 23:44.339
Okay?

23:52.389 --> 23:53.390
What's this about?

23:55.100 --> 23:57.102
What kind of reason are you putting?

23:58.019 --> 23:59.813
It's in-school violence.

23:59.896 --> 24:03.066
By Park Yeon-jin, Lee Sa-ra,
Choi Hye-jeong, and Son Myeong-o.

24:05.694 --> 24:07.696
And you just stood there,
watching it happen.

24:07.779 --> 24:09.197
You shut that lying mouth of yours.

24:09.281 --> 24:11.283
Did they break an or a leg?

24:11.783 --> 24:13.827
You're walking around fine
with nothing broken.

24:13.910 --> 24:17.205
So what bullying is it?
What did I do wrong, huh?

24:17.706 --> 24:19.499
At this point, you're delusional.

24:20.000 --> 24:22.544
Once in a while,
friends hit each other too, no?

24:22.627 --> 24:23.587
Why…

24:25.589 --> 24:26.923
are you okay with that?

24:28.758 --> 24:29.593
What?

24:29.676 --> 24:32.721
You were so proud
that your son got into university.

24:35.182 --> 24:38.602
Would it be fine if your son's friends
hit him as hard as they could?

24:41.188 --> 24:44.065
[Mr. Kim sighs]
I've been trying to go easy on you.

24:44.816 --> 24:47.152
But now you're asking for it.

24:47.736 --> 24:49.196
I can't believe you.

24:50.822 --> 24:51.907
What'd you say

24:53.783 --> 24:54.784
about…

24:56.036 --> 24:57.037
my son?

24:57.120 --> 24:59.664
Say it again! What?

24:59.748 --> 25:01.124
-Say it!
-[man] Stop! That's enough.

25:02.792 --> 25:03.627
Say it.

25:03.710 --> 25:06.838
-What'd you say? Get up! Say it again!
-Mr. Kim! Mr. Kim!

25:06.922 --> 25:08.381
-I dare you.
-[man] It's not worth it.

25:08.465 --> 25:10.091
Come on! Get up!

25:10.634 --> 25:12.260
I dare you to say it again.

25:13.720 --> 25:15.430
-Say it! Come on!
-Mr. Kim!

25:15.514 --> 25:18.099
NEW WORLD HAIR SALON
NO PARKING

25:18.183 --> 25:20.268
[phone ringing]

25:20.352 --> 25:22.437
Ms. Jeong, phone's ringing.

25:23.522 --> 25:24.523
Yeah, coming!

25:25.440 --> 25:27.692
-Oh, hey! Watch it.
-[man] What's wrong?

25:28.401 --> 25:29.903
Just wait a sec.

25:31.029 --> 25:32.030
[Ms. Jeong grunts]

25:36.284 --> 25:37.536
Hi, who is this?

25:39.704 --> 25:40.705
Yeah.

25:42.874 --> 25:44.459
I'm her mom. Yeah.

25:46.503 --> 25:47.671
Who is this?

25:58.598 --> 26:01.518
Go ahead, open it. It's quite all right.

26:04.688 --> 26:06.898
Oh my God, oh my God, oh my God.

26:07.983 --> 26:08.817
CASHIER'S CHECK

26:09.943 --> 26:13.363
And all I need is the father's signature.

26:13.446 --> 26:15.532
Ah, technically, I'm not.

26:16.032 --> 26:18.118
But I… I'm sort of like her father--

26:18.618 --> 26:21.288
Then… you can sign it.

26:21.371 --> 26:23.415
-Ah.
-[Mr. Kim] Yeah.

26:23.498 --> 26:24.624
SETTLEMENT LETTER

26:24.708 --> 26:28.128
As you know,
certain things need to be on file.

26:29.170 --> 26:32.299
I don't… have a signature.

26:32.382 --> 26:34.175
Can I just write my name?

26:34.259 --> 26:35.343
Of course, you can.

26:35.427 --> 26:36.761
VICTIM : JEONG MI-HEE

26:36.845 --> 26:39.848
[Mr. Kim] Just write your name there,
and then write one more thing for us.

26:39.931 --> 26:41.933
-Write what?
-It's just… It's real short.

26:42.017 --> 26:43.893
"Maladjustment."

26:44.644 --> 26:46.646
[suspenseful music playing]

26:47.480 --> 26:49.399
LONG-TERM STAY AVAILABLE

26:52.694 --> 26:55.155
[distressing music playing]

27:00.619 --> 27:01.870
[woman] Honey, forget something?

27:02.954 --> 27:05.457
You… didn't know she left?

27:06.458 --> 27:08.752
Your mother checked out of here
this morning.

27:09.502 --> 27:12.505
Oh, Jesus Christ. Your school uniform.

27:13.965 --> 27:15.550
I'm sure she'll call you.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.385
She's your mother.

27:20.388 --> 27:21.389
My god…

27:23.600 --> 27:25.935
SPACE GROUP OF KOREA BUILDING
SOCIETY AND SPACE

27:43.495 --> 27:45.830
REASON FOR DROPPING OUT
MALADJUSTMENT

27:46.706 --> 27:48.750
GUARDIAN JEONG MI-HEE
PRINCIPAL OF SUNGHAN HIGH SCHOOL

27:48.833 --> 27:51.961
KIMBAP PARADISE

27:52.045 --> 27:54.506
[melancholy music playing]

28:13.733 --> 28:14.734
[birds chirping]

28:17.570 --> 28:18.571
[rain pattering]

28:27.706 --> 28:28.707
[wind whistling]

28:40.927 --> 28:41.928
[sniffles]

28:52.313 --> 28:53.857
KEEP WATER CLEAN
WHEN YOU ENTER THE POOL

29:03.199 --> 29:04.743
[Dong-eun] My scars were itching,

29:05.368 --> 29:08.037
and I was in so much pain
from my period cramps.

29:09.748 --> 29:11.124
So I thought,

29:13.293 --> 29:15.170
"The pharmacy opens at 9:00 a.m.,

29:16.045 --> 29:18.339
and the Han River is
just 20 minutes away."

29:19.549 --> 29:21.050
"The water will be freezing,

29:22.093 --> 29:24.262
but then it'll pass."

29:24.888 --> 29:26.765
"My scars won't itch anymore."

29:28.183 --> 29:29.517
"What more can I want?"

29:31.144 --> 29:32.771
"This is the right thing to do."

29:34.355 --> 29:35.857
[waves lapping]

29:38.276 --> 29:40.278
[melancholy music continuing]

29:41.446 --> 29:42.322
[pants]

29:42.405 --> 29:43.406
[grunts]

29:48.495 --> 29:49.496
[whimpers]

29:51.664 --> 29:52.791
[weeping]

30:34.749 --> 30:36.417
[Yeon-jin] Is Dong-eun pretty?

30:37.335 --> 30:38.670
I mean, what do you think?

30:38.753 --> 30:40.129
From a guy's view point?

30:40.213 --> 30:41.214
[boy clicks tongue]

30:42.173 --> 30:43.091
I don't know.

30:43.591 --> 30:44.592
Don't play dumb.

30:47.011 --> 30:49.472
I mean, her face isn't
the only thing that's pretty.

30:50.431 --> 30:52.183
Maybe you should've just
kept your mouth shut.

30:52.267 --> 30:53.476
Ugh. Get off me.

30:55.687 --> 30:58.022
[Yeon-jin] Where are you going?
Getting more drinks?

30:58.606 --> 30:59.732
Hye-jeong'll do it.

31:01.150 --> 31:02.569
She would've asked me already.

31:02.652 --> 31:04.988
I've gotta go to an early service.

31:05.071 --> 31:08.449
Ugh, my dad threatened
to destroy my studio if I didn't show up.

31:09.242 --> 31:11.870
He wanted me to bring you guys,
since it's for college exams,

31:11.953 --> 31:12.912
but I said no.

31:12.996 --> 31:15.999
Hey, wanna make sure I'm never invited?

31:16.499 --> 31:18.126
Got any white shirts?

31:18.209 --> 31:19.627
[congregation] Amen!

31:21.296 --> 31:23.381
[pastor] Jesus Christ once said,

31:24.465 --> 31:27.051
"If someone slaps your right cheek,

31:27.135 --> 31:29.804
you should let them
slap the left one, too."

31:29.888 --> 31:30.805
[all] Amen!

31:30.889 --> 31:32.807
And if someone takes your shirt,

31:32.891 --> 31:34.767
you should give them your jacket as well.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.227
[congregation] Amen!

31:36.311 --> 31:38.688
And if someone
makes you walk five kilometers,

31:38.771 --> 31:40.648
then you go walk ten kilometers.

31:40.732 --> 31:42.150
Amen! Amen!

31:42.233 --> 31:44.611
-We believe in Jesus Christ.
-Amen! Amen!

31:45.987 --> 31:47.739
Sa-ra's dad's voice cracked.
It was so funny.

31:47.822 --> 31:49.657
You should've seen him.

31:49.741 --> 31:51.993
Maybe he was just shocked
by your small titties, you know?.

31:54.996 --> 31:56.873
-Get me chocolate milk.
-Huh?

31:59.876 --> 32:00.710
Sure.

32:02.253 --> 32:04.255
-Anyone else?
-[Yeon-jin] Hye-jeong!

32:05.048 --> 32:06.716
I told you, I'm fasting.

32:07.383 --> 32:08.885
-[girl weeping]
-Shit.

32:11.137 --> 32:12.597
Hey, Gyeong-ran,

32:12.680 --> 32:14.557
You gonna keep crying all night long?

32:14.641 --> 32:17.018
Stop. Stop crying, you whore.

32:17.602 --> 32:19.854
Fuck, you're so goddamn loud.

32:20.605 --> 32:22.023
[Myeong-o sighs, chuckles]

32:23.399 --> 32:24.567
Shh, Gyeong-ran.

32:24.651 --> 32:25.944
If you scream again…

32:26.527 --> 32:27.403
Huh?

32:34.827 --> 32:35.662
Dong-eun?

32:51.219 --> 32:53.262
[tense music playing]

32:54.764 --> 32:55.598
[chuckles wryly]

32:56.099 --> 32:59.143
Is she crazy? She came here on her own?

33:03.815 --> 33:06.567
Wow, Dong-eun…

33:08.319 --> 33:10.154
I've really missed you.

33:10.989 --> 33:12.740
You dropped out without saying goodbye.

33:13.491 --> 33:16.744
Your dream that you wrote,
on your Cyworld.

33:16.828 --> 33:19.998
A wise mother and a wife.
That's really your dream?

33:20.081 --> 33:23.167
Seriously? Did you really write that?

33:23.251 --> 33:25.378
[derisive laughter]

33:25.461 --> 33:28.715
You shit. Why are you
bringing this up out of nowhere?

33:29.215 --> 33:30.758
[Dong-eun] Sa-ra wants to paint.

33:30.842 --> 33:32.635
Jae-jun wants to inherit the golf course.

33:32.719 --> 33:34.512
Hye-jeong wants to be a stewardess.

33:35.096 --> 33:37.640
And you want to be a wise mother and wife?

33:38.516 --> 33:40.476
[Myeong-o] Hey, what the fuck?

33:40.560 --> 33:42.353
Forget me? Huh?

33:42.437 --> 33:45.023
I have a dream, too.
I'm going to be filthy rich.

33:45.523 --> 33:47.400
A dream? No, I don't need that.

33:48.526 --> 33:51.487
Having a dream is
just for people like… like you,

33:52.488 --> 33:54.282
or him, or her.

33:54.782 --> 33:58.453
With my money, I can pay you
to make my dream job come true. [chuckles]

33:59.245 --> 34:01.581
I don't need a dream. I need nothing.

34:01.664 --> 34:03.833
Maybe a job that's not too shabby.

34:05.126 --> 34:08.046
Um, I'll just get married
while I'm still young and pretty.

34:08.129 --> 34:11.799
I'll pick a nice guy to marry.
Maybe have a kid or two.

34:12.842 --> 34:14.719
A happily ever after of my own.

34:14.802 --> 34:18.639
There isn't a word
to describe all that, is there?

34:19.140 --> 34:20.224
Uh, yeah, there is.

34:20.892 --> 34:21.893
Dumb!

34:21.976 --> 34:23.311
Shut the fuck up, Sa-ra.

34:24.395 --> 34:26.439
Scary. [simpering chuckle]

34:28.816 --> 34:29.817
Tell me.

34:31.652 --> 34:33.154
What's your dream then?

34:35.198 --> 34:36.199
It's you.

34:38.910 --> 34:40.578
You are what I dream about.

34:42.205 --> 34:43.122
I hope

34:44.665 --> 34:46.334
we'll meet again, Yeon-jin.

34:50.296 --> 34:51.297
[chuckles wryly]

34:56.302 --> 34:57.804
[Dong-eun continues chuckling]

35:06.687 --> 35:09.732
SUMMER OF 2006

35:40.429 --> 35:42.265
Knock it off with that. Put it away.

35:42.348 --> 35:44.517
Hey! Go easy on her!

35:44.600 --> 35:47.520
Don't you see all the cigarette burns
on her arms and legs?

35:49.147 --> 35:50.148
Just get to work.

35:55.361 --> 35:57.321
[gentle Korean pop song playing]

36:02.743 --> 36:04.662
[man singing in Korean]

36:09.876 --> 36:11.210
GED EXAM RESULTS

36:16.174 --> 36:19.427
MOON DONG-EUN
YOU HAVE PASSED THE GED EXAM

36:37.361 --> 36:39.906
FALL OF 2006

36:44.660 --> 36:46.495
SCHOLASTIC ABILITY TEST WORKBOOK

36:57.506 --> 37:00.676
FALL OF 2007

37:22.031 --> 37:26.410
FALL OF 2008

37:49.475 --> 37:51.394
[bell ringing]

37:56.983 --> 37:59.610
[gentle Korean pop song continuing]

38:07.451 --> 38:08.661
[woman] Excuse me, Miss…

38:14.083 --> 38:16.419
I'm sorry, but I don't mean to bother you.

38:17.795 --> 38:22.300
Um… I'm twenty years old,
and my name is Gu Seong-hui.

38:22.800 --> 38:26.387
I heard you were leaving the factory
at the end of the month, miss.

38:26.887 --> 38:29.348
So I wanted to have
a talk with you, maybe,

38:29.432 --> 38:31.684
at least before you leave for good.

38:33.894 --> 38:35.730
I'm glad you did. Also, thanks.

38:36.731 --> 38:37.732
What for?

38:38.441 --> 38:39.275
Tip-toeing in.

38:40.151 --> 38:42.236
Oh, you noticed that…

38:42.820 --> 38:44.822
Anyway, congrats to you!

38:44.905 --> 38:47.408
I heard you got accepted into college.

38:47.950 --> 38:49.910
[sighs] You must be so happy!

38:49.994 --> 38:53.414
In college, you can meet new people,
get a boyfriend… [chuckles]

38:56.625 --> 38:57.626
I can't do that.

38:58.419 --> 39:01.922
I'm there because I really need
to go somewhere.

39:02.506 --> 39:04.342
Oh. Where are you going, then?

39:06.093 --> 39:07.094
Samsung?

39:07.803 --> 39:08.637
Hyundai?

39:15.811 --> 39:17.396
[Dong-eun] I wasn't kidding, Yeon-jin.

39:18.147 --> 39:21.984
Ever since that day,
you've been my only dream.

39:22.068 --> 39:26.739
SUNGWU TEXTILE

39:26.822 --> 39:27.907
SPRING OF 2009

39:27.990 --> 39:31.452
What's the strongest coffee you have?
And iced, please. I'm exhausted.

39:31.535 --> 39:33.954
[barista] How's an iced Americano
with an extra shot sound?

39:34.038 --> 39:36.624
Uh, sure. Can I get one?

39:39.168 --> 39:42.254
You can pick it up at the next counter.
Next customer, please.

39:45.674 --> 39:48.094
One black and a mocha latte.

39:48.177 --> 39:51.222
For the latte, a ton of whipped cream
and extra chocolate drizzle.

39:51.305 --> 39:54.225
We'll pay separately, but can you stamp
for both of these on my punch card?

39:54.308 --> 39:57.019
[boy 1] I knew you'd do that.
That's why I didn't bring my wallet.

39:57.103 --> 40:00.439
[barista] Pick up your drinks
at the counter. Who's next?

40:00.523 --> 40:01.816
Please step forward.

40:02.942 --> 40:04.860
[boy 1] I'm saving up.
Every little bit helps.

40:04.944 --> 40:07.446
So, then your punch card'll
turn into diamonds?

40:07.530 --> 40:10.074
-How's a punch card gonna make me rich?
-Come on, share the wealth.

40:10.157 --> 40:12.243
You always do this. Make me pay for you.

40:12.326 --> 40:14.328
-Why can't you pay for your own?
-Sorry…

40:15.579 --> 40:17.706
[boy 1] At least
you're one more stamp to becoming rich.

40:17.790 --> 40:19.542
The punch card can't help me do that.

40:19.625 --> 40:21.794
-How would they even do that?
-Hey, come on.

40:21.877 --> 40:24.171
WELCOME, FRESHMEN OF 2009!

40:25.256 --> 40:28.676
EUICHEON UNIVERSITY OF EDUCATION

40:37.726 --> 40:40.104
[Dong-eun] I think about it
every day, Yeon-jin.

40:41.313 --> 40:42.940
Where would I see you again?

40:44.984 --> 40:46.694
I'm guessing that you have it all.

40:47.695 --> 40:49.864
There's probably nothing
that you're scared of.

40:51.031 --> 40:52.491
So where should we meet

40:53.200 --> 40:54.618
where you'll fear me,

40:54.702 --> 40:56.620
even for just a second?

40:58.622 --> 41:00.791
There is only one place
that I can think of.

41:02.501 --> 41:06.464
In that gym where we were together.
Sixty square meters to share.

41:06.547 --> 41:09.091
HA YE-SOL

41:09.175 --> 41:12.178
Wow, just like a fairy tale.

41:13.846 --> 41:14.805
[Dong-eun] And now,

41:15.306 --> 41:17.641
I'll use your precious hair iron
against you.

41:18.476 --> 41:22.480
The one who is so soft,
with such fair skin.

41:23.772 --> 41:25.232
My story's like a fairy tale?

41:25.316 --> 41:29.528
Yeah. But since my mommy's
not the hero, I don't like it.

41:30.821 --> 41:32.156
What makes you think that?

41:32.239 --> 41:34.909
Because my mommy has lots of money.

41:34.992 --> 41:37.912
Main characters are
supposed to have nothing at all.

41:37.995 --> 41:40.748
[dark, somber music playing]

41:40.831 --> 41:42.249
No, that's not true.

41:43.167 --> 41:45.628
In this story,
your mother is the main character.

41:47.171 --> 41:50.341
That's because this story isn't

41:51.425 --> 41:52.343
a fairy tale.

41:56.013 --> 41:57.473
[woman] Fog is denser

41:57.556 --> 42:00.601
when the visibility range is
less than a kilometer.

42:00.684 --> 42:03.938
The fog warning issues yesterday
is still in effect today.

42:04.021 --> 42:07.942
Did you know that fog can even
potentially pose a risk for planes

42:08.025 --> 42:10.528
even greater than a typhoon or lightning?

42:10.611 --> 42:12.863
[Dong-eun] If you love thy neighbor
like you love thy self…

42:12.947 --> 42:14.865
[praying indistinctly]

42:15.824 --> 42:18.619
[Yeon-jin] Although the accidents are
more likely to occur on sunny days,

42:18.702 --> 42:21.622
the fatality rate is
the highest on foggy days.

42:21.705 --> 42:24.083
That's why it's important
to be careful of the fog.

42:24.166 --> 42:25.167
Park Yeon-jin signing out.

42:25.251 --> 42:26.085
FOG WARNING

42:30.256 --> 42:31.715
[Dong-eun] An eye for an eye,

42:32.383 --> 42:33.717
a tooth for a tooth.

42:34.385 --> 42:36.053
A scar for a scar.

42:37.304 --> 42:40.766
The one who injured
shall suffer the same injury.

42:42.393 --> 42:43.727
Well, maybe not.

42:45.563 --> 42:49.066
Then I would be playing too fair,

42:50.651 --> 42:51.569
don't you think?

42:52.945 --> 42:54.947
[somber music swelling]

43:04.957 --> 43:06.959
[dark, moody Korean pop song playing]
